From 8135cd91bfbc437f9323a969d981cf052fea13a2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 2 Aug 2026 15:57:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] iommu/vsi: propagate the register mapping error from
 probe

devm_platform_ioremap_resource() returns an ERR_PTR describing why the
mapping failed, but vsi_iommu_probe() replaces every failure with
-ENOMEM. A missing or busy register range is then reported as an
allocation failure, and -EPROBE_DEFER is lost, so a probe that should
have been retried fails permanently instead.

Return the error the helper produced.

Fixes: 917ace84b770 ("iommu: Add verisilicon IOMMU driver")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Yi Ding <yi.s.ding@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c b/drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c
index 42c424496d073..edb0c43087a26 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/vsi-iommu.c
@@ -682,7 +682,7 @@ static int vsi_iommu_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	iommu->regs = devm_platform_ioremap_resource(pdev, 0);
 	if (IS_ERR(iommu->regs))
-		return -ENOMEM;
+		return PTR_ERR(iommu->regs);
 
 	iommu->num_clocks = devm_clk_bulk_get_all(dev, &iommu->clocks);
 	if  (iommu->num_clocks < 0)
